.TH SCS-CLTMANAGER 1 "October 2026" "sslcrtsrv 0.9.7" "SSLCrtSrv Manual"
.SH NAME
scs-cltmanager \- manage SSLCrtSrv client registrations and permissions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B scs-cltmanager
.RI [ \-\-config " " \fIPATH\fR ]
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B scs-cltmanager
is a server-side administration tool for client registrations: confirming or
revoking clients, and granting or revoking their access to certificates.
Running it with no subcommand at all lists unconfirmed client registrations.
.TP
.BI "\-\-config " PATH
Default
.IR /etc/sslcrtsrv/server_config.json .
Only relevant if the server being managed runs with a non-default config \(em
it is what
.B confirm
reads to compute the server's own fingerprint for the identity-verification
step, and what relocates the database lookup to that config's data directory
if one is set.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B listall
Short overview of every client.
.TP
.BI "list " "[client_id]"
Every client and their certificate permissions, or just one client's if
given.
.TP
.BI "registration_command " "[client_id] [\-\-server\-host HOST] [\-\-server\-port PORT]"
Print the
.BR scs-client (1)
.B init
and
.B register
command lines to run on a new client host, built from this server's own
.IR registration_secret / port .
.B \-\-server\-host
is required unless
.I listen_address
is already a concrete, non-wildcard address (not
.IR 0.0.0.0 " or " :: ),
since there is no separate "public hostname" field to read one from
automatically.
.I client_id
is embedded via
.B \-\-client\-id
if given; omit it to let the new client default to its own hostname. The
registration secret is embedded directly in the printed
.B init
line for one-line convenience, which will appear in the new host's shell
history and process listing \(em omit that flag from the printed command
(so
.BR scs-client (1)
prompts for it interactively instead) if that matters for a given
deployment.
.TP
.BI "confirm " client_id
Confirm a pending registration \(em prompts for interactive yes/no after
showing both public-key fingerprints, so the fingerprint can be verified
out-of-band before confirming.
.TP
.BI "acme_confirm " client_id
Confirm a pending ACME account (a client registered via
.BR scs-acme-server (1)'s
newAccount endpoint, rather than
.BR scs-client (1)).
Prompts for interactive yes/no after showing the account key's RFC 7638
thumbprint. Unlike
.BR confirm ,
there is no server-side key involved in ACME's own JWS-based authentication,
so only the client's own key fingerprint is shown.
.TP
.BI "revoke " client_id
Un-confirm an already-confirmed client entirely. Not the same as
.B revoke_permission
below.
.TP
.BI "delete " client_id
Delete a client entry outright, after confirmation.
.TP
.BI "assign " "client_id fqdns [\-\-valid\-until DATETIME]"
Grant (or approve) a client's access to a certificate/FQDNs set, whether or
not the client ever requested it itself.
.B \-\-valid\-until
optionally makes the grant expire automatically; omit for one that never
expires.
.TP
.BI "revoke_permission " "client_id fqdns"
Revoke a specific certificate grant, or every grant for that client if
.I fqdns
is
.BR all .
.TP
.BI "set_expiry " "client_id fqdns " "{DATETIME|never}"
Change an already-granted permission's expiry date without touching its
status.
.TP
.BI "clean_requests " "[client_id]"
Bulk-delete pending (unapproved) requests, for one client or every client,
after confirmation.
.TP
.BI "set_allowed_ip " "client_id " "{IP-OR-CIDR|none}"
Set or clear an optional IP-pinning restriction on a client \(em a second
authentication factor on top of the cryptography that already authenticates
every request. Only takes effect for ACME accounts (see
.BR scs-acme-server (1));
the traditional protocol never consults it. Validated as a real IP address or
CIDR network (e.g.
.IR 203.0.113.5 " or " 203.0.113.0/24 )
before being stored;
.B none
clears an existing restriction.
.SH FILES
.I /etc/sslcrtsrv/server_config.json
\(em default configuration file.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR scs-crtmanager (1),
.BR scs-server (1),
.BR scs-admintui (1),
.BR scs-acme-server (1)
.PP
The project's
.I Manual.MD
has the full narrative reference.
.SH AUTHOR
